    "pregnancyCategory": "Discontinue Bempedoic Acid when pregnancy is recognized unless the benefits of therapy outweigh the potential risks to the fetus. There are no available data on Bempedoic Acid use in pregnant women to evaluate for a drug-associated risk of major birth defects, miscarriage, or adverse maternal or fetal outcomes. There is no information regarding the presence of Bempedoic Acid in human or animal milk, the effects of the drug on the breastfed infant, or the effects of the drug on milk production. Breastfeeding is not recommended during treatment with Bempedoic Acid.",
