    "pregnancyCategory": "There are no adequate and well-controlled studies of Prasugrel use in pregnant women. Reproductive and developmental toxicology studies in rats and rabbits at doses of up to 30 times the recommended therapeutic exposures in humans revealed no evidence of fetal harm; however, animal studies are not always predictive of a human response. It is not known whether Prasugrel is excreted in human milk. Because many drugs are excreted in human milk, Prasugrel should be used during nursing only if the potential benefit to the mother justifies the potential risk to the nursing infant.",
